---
title: "gas_fee_computation (Sui Whitepaper: EIP-1559 Style Fees)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_read_gas_info: extract GasInfo from Tx (ObjRef, MaxGas, BaseFee, Tip)
    q_read_gas_info --> q_resolve_gas_obj: resolve gas object from ObjRef (must be Coin of SUI)

    q_resolve_gas_obj --> q_check_balance: check gas object balance >= MaxGas * BaseFee + Tip
    q_check_balance --> q_begin_metering: sufficient balance
    q_check_balance --> q_error_balance: insufficient balance
    q_error_balance --> [*]: return error (transaction rejected)

    q_begin_metering --> q_execute: execute transaction with gas metering
    q_execute --> q_success: execution completes successfully
    q_execute --> q_abort: execution aborts (gas exhausted or runtime error)

    q_success --> q_compute_fee: total_fee = (GasUsed * BaseFee) + Tip
    q_compute_fee --> q_deduct: deduct total_fee from gas object
    q_deduct --> [*]: return SuccessEffects with updated gas object

    q_abort --> q_compute_abort_fee: total_fee = (GasUsed * BaseFee) + Tip
    q_compute_abort_fee --> q_deduct_abort: deduct fee from gas object (effects discarded)
    q_deduct_abort --> [*]: return AbortEffects (fees still charged)

    note right of q_execute
        INV-001: Gas fees always charged regardless of success or abort
        INV-002: BaseFee algorithmically adjusted at epoch boundaries
        INV-003: Tip prioritizes transaction during congestion
        INV-004: Gas object must be Coin of SUI type
    end note
